llama: probe flash attention for a quantized V cache in AUTO mode
Fold-into: upstream/llama-context

The defect

A quantized V cache needs flash attention. With flash_attn_type AUTO, llama_init_from_model
changed the type to ENABLED for a quantized V, thus the probe of the device of each attention
layer (resolve_fused_ops) did not run. When a device cannot run flash attention on the types
and the shapes of a layer, the scheduler then runs FLASH_ATTN_EXT of that layer on the CPU,
with no error and no message. On an accelerator that is a large drop in speed, and the caller
cannot know it.

The change

With AUTO and a quantized V, the context keeps AUTO. The probe runs, and when a layer cannot
run flash attention on its device, the constructor throws "quantized V cache was requested,
but this requires Flash Attention on the device of each attention layer", thus
llama_init_from_model returns null. A caller can then select an F16 cache. ENABLED keeps its
behavior, and DISABLED with a quantized V is an error as before. Thus a caller of AUTO with a
quantized V gets a null context and an error line where it got a context that runs such a
layer on the CPU.

tests/test-kv-quant-auto-fa.cpp makes a Q8_0 K and V context with AUTO on the generated
qwen35-dense model and decodes (the CPU runs flash attention), and expects the creation with
DISABLED to fail. A device that refuses the op is necessary for the failure path of AUTO:
GGML_HEXAGON_OPFILTER=FLASH_ATTN_EXT on HTP0 gives it on the phone.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

